# 19. TWO-PASS AUDIT APPROACH

Conduct two distinct passes.

## PASS 1 — Independent discovery

Inspect, test, reproduce, classify and document all identified issues.

Do not immediately change large areas of code.

Deliver:

- Architecture assessment.
- Functional test matrix.
- Security assessment.
- UX assessment.
- Performance assessment.
- Database assessment.
- Defect register.
- Release readiness evaluation.

This creates an independent baseline.

## PASS 2 — Remediation and verification

After producing the discovery report:

1. Prioritise P0 and P1 issues.
2. Fix confirmed issues in small, isolated changes.
3. Preserve existing product requirements.
4. Add regression tests.
5. Run the affected test suites again.
6. Run full regression tests.
7. Review the changes independently.
8. Document unresolved issues.

Do not perform risky schema changes, production data modifications or deployments without approval.

Do not undertake broad redesigns or major architectural rewrites without explaining the benefit and obtaining approval.

If changes cannot be safely applied, produce precise implementation recommendations rather than making speculative edits.

